div.p:
—the Tories seem now to be somewhat more cautious about continuing a UK presence
                    in the Persian Gulf than earlier speculation, largely for budgetary reasons;
                    consistent with the long history of Tory interest in the Middle East, the Heath
                    Government will probably be more active but even-handed in the Arab-Israel
                    conflict;

—on Rhodesia, the Tories are committed to another effort to negotiate with the
                    Smith regime, though they recognize the prospects for success are slim; the new
                    Government will also work more closely with South Africa;
